Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:19:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 564/564] [DS4.1] Expert scale-code tests follow v2: the pad
 lives in scale_pack, each thread expands its own row

The 127 pad of an uncoded word is written by scale_pack.py, not gemm.py.
v2 expands each thread's own row again, so the 2-bit store is a direct
statement of the narrow-expert test inside the per-thread loop; the test
checks that store, and that the 4-bit branch never reads the 2-bit codes.
The file is formatted, and an unused tile count goes.
